title: TutorialManager_Intro
---
<<lock>>
<<setInternal>>
<<showTutorial "Press SPACE to advance dialogue">>
(It’s 2008 in the town of Naperville, Illinois.)
<<hideTutorial>>
(Your shift just started. It’s 8 PM on a Tuesday.)
(The band next door is playing so loud that the music leaks in through the walls.)
(You recognize the song. STICK YOUR WAND IN MY ASS CALL IT HIGHER EDUCATION by shit-zard lizard wizard.)
(It’s kind of awesome. Your fingers tap along to the lack of a consistent beat.)
(Oop. Looks like my manager's here. Let's talk to him to see what he wants.)
<<setNormal>>
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===

title: TutorialManager
---
<<lock>>
<<setRepeatNode "TutorialManager_Repeat">>
PHYLL: ...
PHYLL: Hiya Lily, how's your first day goin'?
<<showTutorial "Choose dialogue with A/D or arrow keys and SPACE">>
-> Good . . .
-> No one's come to this counter yet.
<<hideTutorial>>
PHYLL: Yeah, pretty slow business so far.
PHYLL: But the freaks in this part of town always start showing up around this time.
PHYLL: No doubt they'll come over for a quick pick-me-up after the show!
PHYLL: In the meantime, why don't you show me what you learned in that fancy magic school of yours?
<<setInternal>>
He's talking about Barvard University of Thaumaturgy and Transmutation, which you totally lied about on your resume.
The only alchemic experience you have is a 20 dollar online witchery course, taught by Madame Legrange of Nevada.
<<setNormal>>
PHYLL: I'm preparing for a long shift, and I gotta pick up my boyfriend after he's done with his affair.
PHYLL: So I could really use a potion to wake me up!
PHYLL: Since you're new here, a few reminders…
PHYLL: You can use your noggin to INSPECT characters, ingredients, and potions to learn more about them.
PHYLL: If you're observant, you might be able to find an even bigger problem to solve for your customers!
PHYLL: Why don't you try INSPECTing me? (HINT: Press 'Q' on my SPRITE!)
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===

title: TutorialManager_Repeat
---
<<lock>>
PHYLL: ...
PHYLL: INSPECT me by pressing Q on my SPRITE!
<<unlock>>
<<stop>>
===

